-- Provisional research briefs, one per new claim.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO public_research_briefs (brief_id,claim_id,revision_number,supersedes_brief_id,quotation_source_url,headline,evidence_strength,test_framing,evidence_summary,prior_information_summary,corpus_warning,missing_gates_json,research_status,as_of_date,created_at) VALUES
  ('brief_tb_2020_22_01_r1','tb-2020-22-01-abortion-and-the-2020-election',1,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bFVnevLGl7s','Weak. A commonplace 2020 sermon line with a 2022 court decision taped on.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? No. “Abortion is on God’s heart” cannot miss. Specificity: Specificity? Extremely low. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: The site does not claim he predicted RBG’s death or a 2022 date. It treats later events as the fruit of “abortion is on God’s heart in this election”: • Sept 18, 2020: Ruth Bader Ginsburg dies. • Sept 29 / Oct 26: Amy Coney Barrett nominated and confirmed. • Oct 17, 2020: Phil Vischer abortion video circulates among Christians. • June 24, 2022: Dobbs overturns Roe. Three of five in the majority are Trump appointees. Analysis: • Every major evangelical outlet in summer 2020 said abortion was the 2020 issue. That is pastoral consensus, not a forecast. • He did not predict Ginsburg’s death. Without that death, Barrett is not on the Court in October 2020. • Dobbs is 22 months after the video. The causal chain (RBG dies -> third Trump justice -> Dobbs) was the standard conservative analysis the week she died. • A Phil Vischer YouTube video is not fulfillment of a prophecy. It is a commentary clip. Verdict: Weak. A commonplace 2020 sermon line with a 2022 court decision taped on.','Predictability: Humanly predictable? Yes. It was the evangelical election frame. Already public: Credit for already public things? Abortion as the 2020 Christian voting issue was public for years. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2020-08-07 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Have a verified human check the original-video segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2020-08-07 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2020_22_02_r1','tb-2020-22-02-russian-oil-price-spike',1,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZidiIdg3U4M','Weak to moderate. Right direction and month on a market that was already coiled.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Partly (Russia + November + up). Specificity: Specificity? Medium on country and month. No price target. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Nov 2, 2020 starts a climb. Archive: Russian grades (Sokol/ESPO) up >30% in November and ~88% Nov 2020-March 2021. Fear-not applied to the election, the first COVID vaccine headlines, and the economy. Vulture = people grasping at leftover Trump-return dates in 2021. Analysis: • Global crude was doing the same thing. WTI went from the COVID crash through a sharp Q4 2020-Q1 2021 recovery on vaccine news and demand hopes. “Russian oil in November” is a slice of a world tape. • September 2020 “don’t listen to reports that oil will keep falling” was a contrarian-sounding line at the end of a historic demand collapse. A November bounce was one of two obvious paths. • The eagle/vulture half is a separate sermon about disappointed Trump supporters – not an oil fact. Verdict: Weak to moderate. Right direction and month on a market that was already coiled. Not unique to Russia.','Predictability: Predictable? A Q4 bounce after the crash was a live debate. Already public: Already public? Oil-recovery talk was public. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2020-09-10 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Have a verified human check the original-video segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2020-09-10 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2020_22_04_r1','tb-2020-22-04-egypt-and-ethiopia-water-war',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-20-22/','Weak. Correct that Egypt did not stop the dam. • Egypt-Ethiopia dam fight had been a headline since ~2011. In late 2020 it was already the standard “water war” example in foreign-policy media.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Soft – “Egypt’s water play fails eventually.” Specificity: Specificity? Country + water + failure. No date, no GERD in the quoted line. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: GERD filling completed ~September 2023. Egypt admits talks failed. Three years after the word. Analysis: • Egypt-Ethiopia dam fight had been a headline since ~2011. In late 2020 it was already the standard “water war” example in foreign-policy media. • “Spending money that won’t work / lose authority” is the pessimistic baseline analysts already used. • No 2020-21 war. The title says “Water War.” The fulfillment is failed talks and a finished dam years later. Verdict: Weak. Correct that Egypt did not stop the dam. That outcome was the default forecast in 2020.','Predictability: Predictable? Yes if you followed GERD. Already public: Already public? The dispute was public for a decade. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2020-12-03 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2020-12-03 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2020_22_05_r1','tb-2020-22-05-january-6th-big-tech-censorship-and',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-20-22/','Weak. A same-week temperature check, later labeled a Jan 6 prophecy.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? The two-year “effects continue” half, no. “Something ugly soon in the U.S.” in that week, barely. Specificity: Specificity? Low. Venezuela + computers + two years. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: • Jan 6, 2021, one week later, treated as the U.S. “mirroring Venezuela.” • Trump banned from social platforms; “online war.” • Ban lasts until Musk / late 2022, filed as the two-year clock. • Venezuela’s crisis continues. Analysis: • Dec 28, 2020 is ten days after the Electoral College vote and in the middle of “Stop the Steal.” Everyone in that information world was already talking upheaval, Venezuela comparisons (“socialist / illegitimate president”), and tech censorship. Jan 6 planning was public enough that the rally was advertised. • “Venezuela + U.S. upheaval + online war” on Dec 28 is the water that audience was swimming in. • Two computer tables = the internet. That vision will match any platform fight. • Venezuela as a two-year clock is unfalsifiable; the country has been in crisis for years before and after. Verdict: Weak. A same-week temperature check, later labeled a Jan 6 prophecy.','Predictability: Predictable? Highly, in that crowd, that week. Already public: Already public? The stolen-election / censorship narrative was the dominant right-media story of December 2020. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2020-12-28 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2020-12-28 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2020_22_06_r1','tb-2020-22-06-tanzanian-president-s-big-lie',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-20-22/','Weak. Named a man the world already called a liar; a later death lie is treated as the reveal.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? “He will be exposed as untrustworthy” is soft. Specificity: Specificity? Named the president. No mechanism. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Magufuli dies March 17, 2021. Government denied he was ill; VP said he was “healthy and working”; people arrested for rumors. Archive treats the cover-up around his death as the unmasking. Analysis: • Magufuli was already internationally infamous as a COVID-denying, authoritarian showman. “Not trustworthy” was the foreign-press consensus in 2020. • The word does not mention illness or death. Death-plus-cover-up is a grim event used to cash a character attack. • Two months later is tight. The content is a reputation that already existed. Verdict: Weak. Named a man the world already called a liar; a later death lie is treated as the reveal. Next was Spain; those entries are now below.','Predictability: Predictable? His reputation was already that. Already public: Already public? Yes – COVID denial, vanished opponents, etc. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2021-01-19 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillmen