  ('brief_tb_2023_17_r1','tb-2023-17-bluegrass-legend-s-death',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-23/','Notable partial. Best 2023 candidate after Luna-25. Shared November 9, 2023 (heard November 4) - Follow-up December 11, 2023 - Terry Baucom died','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Yes, on a short clock. Specificity: Specificity? High for this archive. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Shared November 9, 2023 (heard November 4) - Follow-up December 11, 2023 - Terry Baucom died Verdict: Notable partial. Best 2023 candidate after Luna-25. Still unnamed. Not proof of office.','Predictability: Humanly predictable? Only if the illness was already whispered. Otherwise low base rate. Already public: Already public or scheduled? Death was not scheduled. Illness-publicity remains an open check. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2023-11-09 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2023-11-09 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2023_18_r1','tb-2023-18-speaker-of-the-house-drama',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-23/','Fail. Clearest “already happened, then relabeled” entry of the year.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? A Christmas-adjacent Speaker sign after October’s chaos is almost sure to find a headline. Specificity: Specificity? Office title + holiday window. No named person, no resignation, no vote. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: December 6: McCarthy says he will leave Congress at year-end. December 19: he files resig- nation (two-week notice). Christmas sits in the middle of that window. Archive also points to McCarthy/Gaetz character warfare. Troy’s own follow-up admits Johnson is already Speaker and that McCarthy is merely still in Congress. Analysis: The historically rare event – throwing out a sitting Speaker – was already over. What remained was whether the former Speaker would quit the House. After October 3 that was a live, widely discussed question. “The Speaker of the House” on November 22 denotes Johnson. The archive cashes the word on McCarthy, who was not Speaker when the video went up. Verdict: Fail. Clearest “already happened, then relabeled” entry of the year.','Predictability: Humanly predictable? McCarthy retiring at year-end was an obvious next chapter. Already public: Already public? The ouster, Johnson’s election, and McCarthy’s lame-duck status were all public. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2023-11-22 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Capture the verbatim original wording; none is quoted in the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2023-11-22 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO public_research_briefs (brief_id,claim_id,revision_number,supersedes_brief_id,quotation_source_url,headline,evidence_strength,test_framing,evidence_summary,prior_information_summary,corpus_warning,missing_gates_json,research_status,as_of_date,created_at) VALUES
  ('brief_tb_2023_19_r1','tb-2023-19-christmas-massacre',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-23/','Tragic real event; low prophetic difficulty. Weak as a test of hearing.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? “Christmas massacre” somewhere on the persecuted-church map is not tight. Nigeria is the highest- probability country for that sentence. Specificity: Specificity? Depends on the unearthed original sentence. Archive presentation is event-first. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Fulani militia attacks on Christian communities in Plateau State, Nigeria, beginning about December 23, 2023; death toll reported in the 160-200 range; churches and homes burned; timed around Christmas. Communities had received written warnings they “will not celebrate Christmas.” Analysis: Christmas-season massacres of Christians in Nigeria’s Middle Belt are a recurring pattern, docu- mented year after year. Predicting Christian deaths at Christmas in Nigeria in mid-December is predicting a known seasonal atrocity class. The original December 13 wording is thinner in the public archive extract than most entries; the result paragraph does most of the work. Ten days from video to attack looks impressive until the base rate is included. Verdict: Tragic real event; low prophetic difficulty. Weak as a test of hearing.','Predictability: Humanly predictable? As a class, yes. Already public: Already public? The pattern and warning letters were public. The specific December 23 wave was not dated on December 13. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2023-12-13 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2023-12-13 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2023_20_r1','tb-2023-20-cheese-contamination',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy','Fail as prediction. Outbreak illness onsets ran October 18, 2023 through February 5, 2024.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Food-outbreak words almost always find a later FDA bulletin. Specificity: Specificity? Unknown-tight in the year-page extract; class is common. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Multistate E. coli O157:H7 outbreak linked to RAW FARM raw cheddar; 11 cases in five states; February 16, 2024 public alert and recall. The company later disputed the link and lifted the recall. Analysis: Outbreak illness onsets ran October 18, 2023 through February 5, 2024. People were already sick two months before the December 20 video. What February added was public attribution to RAW FARM cheddar, not the start of the contamination. RAW FARM / Organic Pastures already had a long recall history, including raw-milk Campylobacter in May 2023 and unpasteurized-cheese Salmonella in August 2023. “Raw cheese will make people sick” is an industry-risk sentence. Verdict: Fail as prediction.','Predictability: Humanly predictable? Raw-milk/cheese outbreaks are frequent. Already public: Already public? The illnesses were in progress. The branded outbreak announcement was not. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2023-12-20 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Capture the verbatim original wording; none is quoted in the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2023-12-20 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2024_01_r1','tb-2024-01-california-farming-problems',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-24/','Weak match. This appears to be a retrofitted interpretation of routine California weather impacting agriculture rather than a clear, specific prophecy.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Somewhat—specific timing and location, but the imagery is vague. Specificity: How specific was the original word? Low—vague vision with one timeline. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Website: On Feb 5, 2024 (nine days before Valentine''s Day), Gov. Newsom declared a state of emergency for flooding in 8 Southern California counties due to atmospheric rivers. This caused crop loss, erosion, and highlighted needs for better water management and growing techniques (interpreted as "raised garden beds"). the video closely—no major additions or omissions in the core vision. Analysis: confirm Feb 2024 flooding and ag impacts, but the prophecy emphasized "future improvements in technology" and positive growth (tall carrots), while the fulfillment is about destructive flooding and problems. Timing is close but the tone and details don''t align well—flooding isn''t a technological improvement in farming. Overall Verdict: Weak match. This appears to be a retrofitted interpretation of routine California weather impacting agriculture rather than a clear, specific prophecy. The symbolic vision doesn''t naturally point to flooding emergencies. 2.​ Previously reviewed in another document','Predictability: Humanly predictable? Yes, California has well-known water issues, recurring atmospheric rivers, and ongoing farming challenges. Already public: Claims credit for already public/scheduled things? No, but weather patterns aren''t surprising. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2024-01-04 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2024-01-04 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2024_03_r1','tb-2024-03-nikki-haley-s-loss',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-24/','This one lands as a correct prediction, but the human predictability factor is high.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Yes. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: The word was published before most states'' primary elections and accurately predicted her failure to win the Republican nomination. "Scraping along" is presented as describing her campaign hanging on as long as possible.Assessment: The prophecy correctly called that Haley would fail and drop out. However, as you pointed out, this was highly predictable. Running for a major party nomination requires massive funding, and without strong polling or delegate wins, donors dry up fast. By late January, after early contests, her path was already extremely narrow. Most political analysts expected her to drop out soon after Super Tuesday if she kept losing. Overall Verdict: This one lands as a correct prediction, but the human predictability factor is high. It doesn''t require supernatural insight to foresee a struggling candidate running out of money and support.','Predictability: Humanly predictable? Very much so. Campaign finance realities and polling trends made her exit foreseeable. Already public: Specificity? Moderate on the outcome, low on details. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2024-01-29 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2024-01-29 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2024_04_r1','tb-2024-04-oklahoma-earthquake-from-january-31st-2024',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-24/','This is a weak example. While the timing and general location are impressive, the actual event doesn''t match the dramatic vision described.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Is it falsifiable? Partially — a specific quake in Oklahoma could be verified, but the vague visionary language makes it hard to clearly disprove. Specificity: How specific was the original word? Moderately specific on location (Oklahoma + region), but very vague on timing and exact nature of the event. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Website Two days later, on February 2, 2024, a 5.1 magnitude earthquake struck near Oklahoma City — one of the largest in the state''s recent history. Shaking was felt across multiple states. Troy presents this as direct fulfillment of the word given just days earlier. Website Version The archive entry is consistent with the video but condenses it. It keeps the core imagery of moving land and the Oklahoma connection while noting a broader regional impact and societal infrastructure implications. No major additions or omissions stand out. Analysis: Links point to news articles about the quake. The timing is accurate (two days after the video). However, the original vision described dramatic land movement like a landslide or churning mud swallowing entire areas — the actual quake caused minimal damage with no major landslides or landscape changes reported. The "larger reach" and "infrastructures of society" elements are not clearly addressed in the fulfillment. Overall Verdict: This is a weak example. While the timing and general location are impressive, the actual event doesn''t match the dramatic vision described. The fulfillment relies heavily on retrofitting a minor earthquake to a much more intense-sounding prophecy. It follows a common pattern in the archive: vague enough to claim hits, but lacking the precision and scale that would make it compelling.','Predictability: Was it humanly predictable? Oklahoma has frequent small earthquakes due to wastewater injection from oil and gas. A notable quake was plausible. Already public: Does he claim credit for things already public or scheduled? No — the video was posted before the quake. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2024-01-31 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Capture the verbatim original wording; none is quoted in the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2024-01-31 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2024_05_r1','tb-2024-05-trump-stock',1,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OR9fQxSxuXU','Partial overlap with public events. Retrofitted. The links confirm a real merger and initial pop — that part is factual.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Is it falsifiable? Only partly. “Only going to go up” is falsifiable, but he later limited it to the debut pop, making it harder to fail. Specificity: How specific was the original word? Low. No ticker, no date, no company name. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Troy says the March 2024 DWAC merger, Truth Social going public, and the first-day 16% jump fulfill the word. He states he has no further prediction on the stock and warns people not to use this as investment advice. The archive quotes the words accurately but adds a lot after the fact: ●​ Full merger narrative and price timeline ($25 → $43 → $61) ●​ Claim that the going-public event fulfills it ●​ Troy’s later admission that he was wrong to call it figurative What’s missing: The original video’s strong emphasis that it was metaphorical, and that the stock lines were a small side comment, not the main point. Analysis: The links confirm a real merger and initial pop — that part is factual. However: ●​ The merger had been public news for years. ●​ The stock had already jumped hard in January (after DeSantis dropped out) before Troy posted the video. ●​ “Only going to go up” didn’t hold — the stock later dropped sharply, and commenters called him out on it. ●​ He redefined success to just the debut pop so the prophecy couldn’t be wrong. Overall Assessment He said “Trump stock is only going to go up” before the ticker change, and the stock did pop on debut. That’s the strongest part. But the merger was already expected, the price had already risen before he spoke, he first called it figurative, and he later narrowed the claim once the stock started falling. It reads like a vague comment on a known story that got retrofitted after a short-term spike. Overall Verdict: Partial overlap with public events. Retrofitted. Not a clean or impressive fulfillment. The archive presents it as a hit, but the details show a vague remark on a known story that was later reshaped to fit the outcome.','Predictability: Was it humanly predictable? Yes. The SPAC merger was long-awaited and heavily discussed in the media. Already public: Does he claim credit for things that were already public or scheduled? Yes. The merger timeline was known. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2024-02-14 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Have a verified human check the original-video segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2024-02-14 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2024_06_r1','tb-2024-06-5-day-reversal-january-6th-lies',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-24/','This is a classic example of vague language being retrofitted to a political event after it happened.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Is it falsifiable? No — “reversals” and “breakthroughs” are too vague. Specificity: How specific was the original word? Extremely low — just “reversals” and “breakthroughs” in five days. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: the general “reversals” and “things undone” to the release of hidden testimony that contradicted the prior J6 committee report. The archive entry adds the specific title linking it to “January 6th Lies” and claims fulfillment through House committee releases of hidden January 6 transcripts and reports on March 8 and March 11, 2024. These releases undermined the original J6 committee’s narrative, particularly around Trump offering 10,000 National Guard troops. significantly adds the January 6 connection and specific political fulfillment. The original video did not mention January 6, transcripts, or any specific political event. Overall Verdict: This is a classic example of vague language being retrofitted to a political event after it happened. The original word was too general to be meaningful, and the specific connection to January 6 was not in the video. It doesn’t hold up as a genuine prophetic word.','Predictability: Was it humanly predictable? Yes — political committees regularly release documents, especially in an election year. Already public: Does he claim credit for things already public or scheduled? The releases appear to have been part of ongoing congressional work. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2024-03-06 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2024-03-06 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2024_07_r1','tb-2024-07-the-death-of-a-wrestling-legend',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-24/','This is a weak, vague “prophecy” that only works because wrestling legends eventually pass away — or retire, or finish a match.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Is it falsifiable? Barely — “wrestling legend is through” is extremely broad and could mean retirement, the end of a storyline, or death. Specificity: How specific was the original word? Extremely low — just “a wrestling legend is through.” The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Claims it was fulfilled when Hulk Hogan died on July 24, 2025, at age 71. They call Hogan the most recognizable wrestling star worldwide. wasn’t clear and pointed to a future news event. The archive directly ties it to Hogan’s death over a year later. Overall Verdict: This is a weak, vague “prophecy” that only works because wrestling legends eventually pass away — or retire, or finish a match. Predicting that a famous old wrestler will be “through” someday isn’t impressive. The 16-month gap and lack of any specific detail make this one of the least convincing entries in the archive.','Predictability: Was it humanly predictable? Yes — many aging wrestling legends from the ‘80s era were in poor health. Already public: Does he claim credit for things already public or scheduled? No, but the vagueness makes it easy to attach to any big name. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2024-03-08 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2024-03-08 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2024_08_r1','tb-2024-08-ihopkc-closing-and-cover-up',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-24/','This one’s better than the wrestling legend because it had a tighter timeline and tied into a very public, ongoing story.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Is it falsifiable? Moderately — “split within the church” and “cover-up” are common in church scandals. Specificity: How specific was the original word? Low — vague terms like split and cover-up, plus a celebrity vision that’s a stretch. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: A month later, on April 16, 2024, a leaked recording showed IHOPKC leaders announcing they were closing the church, camps, and university to form a new organization. A Roys Report article framed it as an attempted cover-up to avoid further financial and legal trouble. They also tie in the “Legally Blonde” vision to lawyers and avoiding lawsuits. Overall Verdict: This one’s better than the wrestling legend because it had a tighter timeline and tied into a very public, ongoing story. Still, predicting more trouble at a ministry already embroiled in scandal isn’t exactly bold prophecy. The Reese Witherspoon vision feels like a weird add-on they’re trying to make fit.','Predictability: Was it humanly predictable? Yes — IHOPKC was already in major crisis after the Bickle allegations; more fallout was expected. Already public: Does he claim credit for things already public or scheduled? The core issues were already public; this feels like predicting more trouble in an already troubled ministry. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2024-03-09 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2024-03-09 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
