  ('brief_tb_2025_21_r1','tb-2025-21-august-2025-pandemic',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-25/','Weak. Date shared: July 19, 2025 Original claims • People will say a pandemic is coming, around August and after.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? The “people will say pandemic in August” half, barely. The “God bans the word” half, no. Specificity: Specificity? Medium on month + the word “pandemic.” Low on pathogen and mandate. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Date shared: July 19, 2025 Original claims • People will say a pandemic is coming, around August and after. • They will say “pandemic,” but God will “off-limit the usage of the word so that they cannot say the same lie as before.” • Impression of a governmental rule about what may be called a pandemic. • Archive later admits the mandate piece has not shown up. Claimed fulfillment August 2025 China chikungunya outbreak; forceful local measures; U.S. headlines asking if it could spread; CDC Level 2 travel notice; Dr. Marc Siegel saying it will not be a pandemic (mosquito-borne, not person-to-person). 10 questions 1. Falsifiable? The “people will say pandemic in August” half, barely. The “God bans the word” half, no. 2. Predictable? Summer virus scare headlines are routine. 3. Commentary? COVID-memory politics. 4. Retrofitted? Yes – regional mosquito outbreak plus “it’s not a pandemic” explainers. 5. Already public? Developing China story; U.S. had paused a vaccine in May. 6. Specificity? Medium on month + the word “pandemic.” Low on pathogen and mandate. 7. Admit failures? Partially – no speech mandate yet; file left open. 8. Scale/tone? “Pandemic” vs. a non-human-to-human outbreak. 9. Cherry-pick? Headlines that used the word kept; word-ban parked. 10. Prophesy the claim? August pandemic-talk, yes. Chikungunya