  ('brief_tb_2025_22_r1','tb-2025-22-out-of-the-blue-attack-on',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-25/','Weak to moderate on sector and season. Weak on surprise attack.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? “Oil turmoil Aug-Sep” is wide. Specificity: Specificity? Medium on sector + sea + season. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Date shared: August 2, 2025 (heard July 12; window Aug-Sep) Original claims • Oil-barrel vision; rolling stock; on the sea; sudden attack; prices spike and spiral. • Hunt new resources; good ones locked away. • Hits the broader market. • Arch-rival / enemy from within causes popular uproar. Claimed fulfillment Trump EO 14329 (Aug 6) squeezing buyers of Russian oil; later NATO pressure; Oct 22 Treasury sanctions on major Russian oil firms; ~5% price jump that day; Hungary’s Orban vs. Peter Magyar as “enemy from within.” Stones Policy, not a surprise strike on tankers. Russian-oil pressure was already the administration’s direction. Hungary subplot is a second story. Window quietly runs into October. 10 questions 1. Falsifiable? “Oil turmoil Aug-Sep” is wide. 2. Predictable? Yes. 3. Political commentary? Yes. 4. Retrofitted? Yes. 5. Already public? Yes, as direction. 6. Specificity? Medium on sector + sea + season. 7. Admit failures? No. 8. Scale/tone? “Wham, out of the blue” oversells sanctions. 9. Cherry-pick? Sea/stock kept; kinetic attack dropped. 10. Prophesy the claim? Did not name Russia, India, or Treasury. Verdict: Weak to moderate on sector and season. Weak on surprise attack.','Predictability: Predictable? Yes. Already public: Already public? Yes, as direction. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2025-08-02 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Ha