  ('brief_tb_2026_09_r1','tb-2026-09-irish-beheading-attempt-and-riots',1,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9VsylM7fmVg','Weak to moderate. Better geography than most. • Three-month lag. He allowed “maybe just the song.” • Ireland/UK migrant-crime unrest was already a 2024-26 running story.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Partly (Ireland + filmed violence). The song hedge weakens it. Specificity: Specificity? Medium – Ireland + filmed + old conflict returns. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: June 8, 2026: Sudanese asylum seeker knives a man in Belfast in what looked like an attempted beheading; video goes viral. Next-day riots, attacks on immigrant housing. Commentators invoke the Troubles. Analysis: • Three-month lag. He allowed “maybe just the song.” • Ireland/UK migrant-crime unrest was already a 2024-26 running story. • Distinctive pieces that did show up: Ireland/NI + filmed violence + Troubles echo. • “Slaughterhouse / Bloody Sunday” is heavier than one stabbing plus riots. Verdict: Weak to moderate. Better geography than most. Still a wide net over a known European story.','Predictability: Predictable? Category, yes. This video, no. Already public: Already public? The social conflict was public. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2026-03-17 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Have a verified human check the original-video segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before