  ('brief_tb_2026_10_r1','tb-2026-10-reform-and-restore-winning-u-k',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-26/','Moderate as election commentary. Weak as supernatural surprise.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Yes – if Reform/Restore had flopped. Specificity: Specificity? High on party names + “not majority / token.” The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Reform wins the most English local seats; Restore wins all 10 of its races; Labour/Tories bleed seats; Starmer resigns June 22. Archive reads “token” as: most seats but not most councils. Analysis: Posted six days before a scheduled election he admitted he knew was coming, using party names he admitted he already knew. Polling for a Reform local surge would have been public. The interesting part is the hedge: not a majority, token victory, disappointment. That is more careful than a “landslide” call. Starmer resigning six weeks later is attached as “upending of global leadership.” Verdict: Moderate as election commentary. Weak as supernatural surprise. One of the cleaner political rows because the hedges match the result.','Predictability: Predictable? Largely, as a pre-election commentary. Already public: Already public? Election date and party brands, yes. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2026-05-01 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2026-05-01 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
