  ('brief_tb_2026_15_r1','tb-2026-15-trump-auctioning-off-public-land',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-26/','Moderate. Tight timing, right policy family, inflated metaphor.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? “Trump opens/sells a chunk of public land soon” – yes. Specificity: Specificity? Medium. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Two weeks later: Trump shrinks two national monuments by ~90%, opening 3+ million acres to use/development. Analysis: “Auction” is metaphor for opening land, not a literal gavel. Monument reductions are a known Trump-world conservation fight (echoes of Bears Ears / Grand Staircase). Two-week gap is tight. “Section of the United States” is grandiose for monument boundaries, but the policy type matches. Verdict: Moderate. Tight timing, right policy family, inflated metaphor.','Predictability: Predictable? Directionally, yes. Exact week, no. Already public: Already public? The land-use agenda was public. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2026-06-28 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2026-06-28 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provision