  ('brief_tb_2026_16_r1','tb-2026-16-spain-wins-the-2026-world-cup',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-26/','Methodologically strong type; result not confirmed from pulled text.','preliminary_signal','Whether the July 10, 2026 word “Spain Wins the 2026 World Cup” was fulfilled as spoken. The original wording and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: A sports champion call is one of the few inherently clean tests in the catalog: either Spain lifts the trophy or not. Pulled fulfillment text is thin here. If the archive lists it as fulfilled, Spain won (or the site is claiming a path to the final as “win”). Without a match report in the scrape, score it as testable, not verified in this pass. Verdict: Methodologically strong type; result not confirmed from pulled text.','Whether the claimed event was already public or predictable before July 10, 2026 is not yet assessed. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2026-07-10 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Capture the verbatim original wording; none is quoted in the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2026-07-10 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2026_17_r1','tb-2026-17-three-week-word-indonesia-2026',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-26/','Weak unless a single named event inside 21 days is produced.','preliminary_signal','Whether the August 9, 2026 word “Three-Week Word: Indonesia 2026” was fulfilled as spoken. The original wording and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: Evidence labels on the archive row: earthquakes, Christians in Indonesia, Islam in Indonesia, fires, volcanoes. Same regional disaster-bin used in the 2025 Malaysia 18-month file. A three-week Indonesia clock in a seismically and politically noisy country will usually find a quake, fire, or church story. Verdict: Weak unless a single named event inside 21 days is produced.','Whether the claimed event was already public or predictable before August 9, 2026 is not yet assessed. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2026-08-09 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Capture the verbatim original wording; none is quoted in the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2026-08-09 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('brief_tb_2026_18_r1','tb-2026-18-trump-and-a-mismanagement-of-funds',1,NULL,'https://troyblackvideos.com/prophecy-archive-26/','Weak. Designed to absorb any money criticism. Pre-loaded unfalsifiability: quotes around “caught,” both too-big and not-big, will blow over, maybe not even him.','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Falsifiable? Almost no. Specificity: Specificity? Low once the hedges are included. The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). Archive claim: • Sept 8 Washington Post: 2025 personal $45k “holiday” gifts to three female aides; ethics-lawyer criticism; White House says legal gifts. • Sept 9: “Trump Dividend” – $5,000 to every adult (archive treats this as the “state level” pot). Analysis: Pre-loaded unfalsifiability: quotes around “caught,” both too-big and not-big, will blow over, maybe not even him. “State level” mapped onto a federal payment is sloppy. Personal gifts + a campaign-style dividend are ordinary Trump-term stories. Verdict: Weak. Designed to absorb any money criticism. 2026 year assessment (listed archive rows) Same machine as 2025: • Double-counting (Iran strike used in celebration + war + markets; April 25 used in mentalist + attempt). • Compass rewrite filed as fulfillment (East Coast -> West Coast / Pratt). • Pre-event political reads that anyone watching the calendar could attempt (UK locals six days out; public-land agenda; Trump-Bibi friction). • A few sharper nouns: mentalist, Reform/Restore + token victory, Krick four-week clock, land opened two weeks later. If 2025 was “mood matching,” 2026 is the same plus one literal oddity (Oz the Mentalist) and one honest miss title (East Coast mixup) th…','Predictability: Predictable? Ethics stories and big-check politics, yes. Already public: Already public? Gift ethics and payout talk are perennial. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2026-08-14 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2026-08-14 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z');

-- Southeast Asia oil seed claim: fourth brief revision from the independent review.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO public_research_briefs (brief_id,claim_id,revision_number,supersedes_brief_id,quotation_source_url,headline,evidence_strength,test_framing,evidence_summary,prior_information_summary,corpus_warning,missing_gates_json,research_status,as_of_date,created_at) VALUES
  ('brief_tb_oil_2026_r4','southeast-asia-oil-2021',4,'brief_oil_r3','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZidiIdg3U4M','Archive admits 2021 miss, then refiles 2024 headlines as a delayed hit','material_provisional','Falsifiability: Yes – and 2021 failed. Specificity: Medium (region + next year). The original wording, the claimed fulfillment, and the measure of a hit must be frozen from the original video before any rating.','Independent review by Joshua Harris (September 2026). The archive admits the stated 2021 timing missed: regional production kept falling and no major boom occurred. It then files 2024 “Southeast Asia oil and gas boom” language as delayed fulfillment of a 2021 word. Independent Rystad data reported that Southeast Asian oil and gas output fell from 5.06 million barrels of oil equivalent per day in 2020 to 4.86 million in 2021. The speaker’s archive says the event did not happen in the stated year and says Troy believes he got the timing wrong. Verdict: Miss on the clock, rewritten as a delayed hit. They can admit a wrong year and still not retire the card.','Predictability: Energy-boom talk is perpetual. Already public: Exploration narratives were public. A reproducible prior-information search with a 2020-09-10 cutoff is still required.','This entry comes from the speaker’s “fulfilled prophecies” archive as reviewed by Joshua Harris. Because that archive selects claims described as fulfilled, it cannot by itself show the speaker’s complete track record.','["Confirm the original video URL, then have a verified human check the segment and surrounding context.", "Confirm the quoted wording against the original video; quotes here are transcribed from the independent review.", "Freeze a measurable definition of fulfillment from the original wording before any rating.", "Preserve independent outcome evidence with URLs and access dates.", "Complete a reproducible prior-information receipt with a 2020-09-10 cutoff.", "Get one named human reviewer to make and publish the final decision."]','provisional_research','2026-09-20','2026-09-21T00:00:00.000Z');

